.key
; ISSUE-0037 -- write and delete in RAM:, with no Execute.
;
; Half of ram-stress-c. If this reproduces on its own, the temporary file
; Execute makes for itself is not needed and the defect is in the plain
; create/write/delete path. If it stays quiet while ram-stress-b does not, the
; opposite.
;
; Sizes and name lengths vary within the iteration on purpose: SYS:C and
; SYS:Libs list to different lengths, so the data blocks differ too, not only
; the names.

Echo "[ram-stress-a] start"

Lab loop

Echo "[ram-stress-a] ."

List "SYS:C" NOHEAD FILES TO "T:P" LFORMAT="; %N"
Delete "T:P" QUIET

List "SYS:Libs" NOHEAD FILES TO "T:a" LFORMAT="; %N"
Delete "T:a" QUIET

List "SYS:C" NOHEAD FILES TO "T:a-considerably-longer-name-than-that" LFORMAT="; %N"
Delete "T:a-considerably-longer-name-than-that" QUIET

List "SYS:Devs" NOHEAD FILES TO "T:xy" LFORMAT="; %N"
Delete "T:xy" QUIET

Skip loop BACK
